THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL IN THE CURRENT TREE
----------------------------------------

None is vendored.  The library itself is header-only and has no
dependencies beyond the C++ standard library.

The test suites use GoogleTest (BSD-3-Clause), which CMake fetches at
configure time; it is a build-time test dependency only and no part of
it is redistributed here.

Three classes of thing in the current tree resemble their upstream
counterparts because they cannot do otherwise, and are retained
knowingly:

  * Names, signatures and the required sequence of operations that ISO
    C++ prescribes for the locale facets.
  * Conversion-specifier semantics that POSIX prescribes for strptime
    and strftime: the field bounds, the two-digit-year split, the
    accepted zone-offset forms, the month-length table, and the leap
    rule.
  * The binary layout of glibc's era data, which is read through
    nl_langinfo.  A description of an interface is not an expression of
    it, and PROVENANCE.md records why "rewriting" it is not meaningful.


